# Talion's Messenger: "draw a card, then discard a card. When you discard a card this way, put a +1/+1 counter ..." The counter
# needs a card actually discarded (CR 603.12, 701.9): with nothing in hand there is nothing to discard. Bot2's Notion Thief makes
# each of Bot1's draws but the first in its draw step go to Bot2 instead (CR 614.11), so on turn 3 Bot1 attacks with an empty hand
# (all of it cast), the loot's draw is skipped, nothing is discarded and the Messenger stays a 1/3; Bot2 draws. On turn 5 Bot1 has kept
# the Island it drew for the turn: the loot's draw is skipped again, but it discards the Island and the Messenger gets its counter, a 2/4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Talion's Messenger
Mox Sapphire
Island
Island x12

